MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Are You Dead Yet? and The End of Heartache feel like natural next choices because their heavy riffs, harsh vocals and strong melodies connect closely with my interest in In Flames and Soilwork.",
    "City of Evil and Vol. 3 appeal because I want aggression with memorable melodies; ambitious guitar work and a balance of heaviness and hooks give me reasons to choose them."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Mostasteless misses my current interest in guitar-driven metal, while Take Off Your Pants & Jacket feels too light for what I want on this visit.",
    "Reanimation's remix focus is less appealing than a straightforward heavy album. Korn and Bless the Martyr & Kiss the Child have appealing heaviness, but that alone does not make them my first choices when I want melodic hooks."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in aggressive music seems to have been stretched to include music whose appeal is quite different from the melodic metal I want now.",
    "My earlier lighter rock interests seem to carry too much weight compared with the heavier albums I have explored more recently."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The combination of melodic guitar lines, harsh vocals and memorable choruses matters more to me right now than heaviness by itself.",
    "Several albums can fit my taste without making me want to choose them today; the closest matches to my current melodic metal mood are the ones I would actually pick."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You understood my interest in heavy music, but some choices missed the specific balance of aggression, guitar melody and hooks I want right now."
}
